At the HARD STOP clock: start nothing new. Push nothing unproven. If the part is committed with Step 5 green, push it and end `READY B1604: <sha40>`; if the measurement finished and no edit was due (OUTCOME B, C, D or DROP), end with the `PARTIAL` line the table names; if it is committed but Step 5 is not finished, push nothing and end `PARTIAL B1604: none | done <parts> | not done <parts>`; write the HANDOVER in either unfinished case.

## STANDING LINES
- **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (Step 0b; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). Re-read main first; do not redo a ticket that is already fixed there: say which, with file and line.
- No message to any human. No comment or edit on any PR. **No Jira write** (this kit names none). Never delete (quarantine). No deploy, no `az`, no hosted host or database, no image push. No word added to any file but THE WORDS. Only throwaway containers named `pc-b1604-*`; the demo VM, `hpsm-demo-*` and any hosted database are never touched.
- **Closed lists** (the allowed edits, the paths, the lines you may change): each is stated by its PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP. **Any path outside your PARTITION: STOP and ask.**
- Every sentence you write about a script, a command or a result is checked against the log it describes (the Step 4 table); a sentence you cannot check is not written (STOP).
- `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; never skip a failing step; a control that does not fire is a failure of the harness, never of the claim.
- **Commit rules:** one commit, subject in plain words (for example "Deploy guide: the Route B lines of 0022 say what was measured"). No ticket key, brief number, card id or person's name in any message. Check with `/usr/bin/grep -c -i -E 'B[0-9]{3,4}|PCOMP|Tuesday|Wednesday|Friday'` plus a name scan: count 0, and a planted control counts 1. **The name scan is underscore-aware:** for each name in the project's records (the product owner's first and family names and his deputy's, as `CLARIFICATIONS.md` names them; write them into your scratch scan file, never into a message), use `(?<![A-Za-z])<name>(?![a-z])` with `re.I`. Its control plants `_by_<name>_` and must fire. Run it over the message and every added line. Exactly ONE trailer: the attribution line your own session reminder gives (count 1). No `.env`, no secret; record gitleaks (`scripts/secret-scan.sh` as written, or the pre-commit hook) at the commit. ONE plain push of ONE ref (never `--force`, never `+`). The ref must be absent before the push.
- **Git identity is never overridden.** Use the repo's own configured identity only, as the IDENTITY slot establishes it. Never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`. Your READY section prints `git log --format='%h %ae | %ce'` for every new commit, each equal to that configured email.
- **Landing rule (quote, RELAYED):** `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1799`, C-101 (1): "[the coordinator] squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks. Nothing is deployed (Composer deploys only on your card)" (re-applied in every landing since, e.g. `:2501`). **You push your branch only. Tuesday opens the PR, reads CodeQL first and lands it (head-pinned squash).**

